---
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  heading="About ToolKade"
  title="About ToolKade: Free Tools That Run in Your Browser"
  description="ToolKade builds free, fast online tools for Sri Lanka and beyond. Learn how our tools work, how we keep rates accurate and how we protect your privacy."
>
  <p>
    <strong>ToolKade</strong> ("kade" means shop) is a collection of free online tools. We started with the
    calculators people in Sri Lanka search for every month, such as take-home pay after APIT and EPF, vehicle
    import duty and CEB electricity bills, and we are adding everyday image, PDF, developer and text tools
    alongside them.
  </p>

  <h2>What we believe</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Tools should be free and fast.</strong> No sign-up, no waiting and pages that load quickly on a
      phone with a weak signal.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your data is yours.</strong> Our tools run in your browser. Files you compress and numbers you
      enter are processed on your own device and are never uploaded to our servers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Numbers should be traceable.</strong> Tax brackets, duty rates and tariffs change often. Every
      calculator that depends on official rates shows where those rates come from and the date we last checked
      them.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we keep calculators accurate</h2>
  <p>
    Official rates are kept in separate data files with a link to the source, such as the Inland Revenue
    Department, Sri Lanka Customs or the Public Utilities Commission. When we cannot confirm a figure, the
    calculator says so rather than guessing. Results are still estimates, so please confirm important figures
    with the relevant authority before you rely on them. See our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for
    details.
  </p>

  <h2>How ToolKade is funded</h2>
  <p>
    ToolKade is free to use. We plan to cover our costs with advertising and, later, optional premium features
    such as ad-free use and batch processing. The core tools will stay free.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Found a mistake, a rate that has changed or a tool you would like us to build? We would like to hear from
    you. Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
